<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="JirAI: Work with AI assistants" id="JirAI-AI">

    <primary-label ref="jirai"/>

    <link-summary>What JirAI adds for AI coding assistants: agent skills, agent tools, Markdown docs pushed to Jira and the virtual board.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Give your AI assistant Jira context, push its specs and plans to Jira and approve the changes it asks for.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>JirAI features for AI coding assistants in JetBrains IDEs: agent skills for Claude Code, Codex, Copilot CLI and Junie, agent tools that check drafts against the real create screen, Markdown docs pushed to Jira and a virtual board for the agent's plan.</web-summary>

    <p>
        Besides the everyday Jira work, JirAI helps when an AI coding assistant works on your Jira issues.
        The assistant can check a draft issue against your project before filing it, show its plan on a board in the IDE
        and turn its specs and plans into Jira issues.
        It changes Jira only when you approve the change.
    </p>

    <deflist type="medium">
        <def title="Agent skills">
            Add JirAI's skills to Claude Code, Codex, Copilot CLI and Junie, so the agent uses the virtual board
            and checks a Jira ticket before filing it without being told how.
            See <a href="JirAI-Agent-Skills.topic"/>.
        </def>
        <def title="Agent tools">
            Let the assistant read a project's real create screen and check a draft issue against it and your house
            standard before it files anything.
            See <a href="JirAI-Agent-Tools.topic"/>.
        </def>
        <def title="Push Markdown docs">
            Turn a Markdown spec or plan into a Jira issue and keep the issue description up to date.
            See <a href="JirAI-AI-Workflows.topic"/>.
        </def>
        <def title="Virtual board">
            Watch the agent's plan as live cards in an IDE editor tab, send it notes and approve the Jira changes it
            asks for.
            See <a href="JirAI-Virtual-Board.topic"/>.
        </def>
    </deflist>

    <seealso>
        <category ref="related">
            <a href="JirAI-Agent-Skills.topic"/>
            <a href="JirAI-Agent-Tools.topic"/>
            <a href="JirAI-AI-Workflows.topic"/>
            <a href="JirAI-Virtual-Board.topic"/>
        </category>
    </seealso>
</topic>
